**F1 — high, blocker:** [review_bundle.go:4719](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-581662681/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:4719) treats an unchanged review-plan digest as proof of an unchanged commitment. However, `reviewBundlePlanDigest` hashes review criteria, tools and profiles—not requirements or decisions (lines 1956–1970).

A dependency can change its requirements, receive a new approved review, and retain the same plan digest and governing-contract IDs. This comparison then accepts it and replaces the sealed dependency wholesale. The consumer keeps its old approval despite a changed commitment its reviewer never assessed. Current trust and source approval do not prove continued consumer compatibility.

Preserve and compare the dependency’s semantic commitment, excluding operational follow-up dispositions, and cover a changed-requirements/reapproved-source regression. The existing adversarial corpus does not cover this shortcut.

Independent checks passed: subject binary build, focused tests, broader federated/manifest/retained-child tests, strict artifact check, and strict surface check. The sealed validation report records 228 passing checks. Assessment commands and validation reruns were omitted to preserve the read-only boundary. No repository changes or attestation were made.

Rules applied: `pose-review`, review workflow, backend Go, security, documentation style, and delivery evidence. Knowledge was consulted; no risk was accepted. SD-854e5641 maps to D1, the decision to retain approval across qualifying repins.

